Create new namespace

Burger menu (next to vSphere Client) in the top left
Supervisor Management
Namespaces
New Namespace -> select supervisor -> dns compliant name -> select zones -> finish 

Configure namespace
Summary -> VM Service -> Manage VM Classes -> check all boxes on both pages -> Save
Storage -> Add Storage -> select storage policy -> OK

Create VKS cluster
Resources -> Kubernetes -> Create Cluster 
1. Configuration type -> Cluster API -> Custom Configuration
2. Name cluster -> select VKr version -> select at least "best-effort-medium" size
3. Control plane -> select # of replicas -> photon / ubuntu 
4. Node pools -> select node pool
5. Save / download the yaml & Finish 

Cluster should take ~5 mins to come up 
